id: proverbs-through-the-month
title: Proverbs through the month
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: One chapter of Proverbs a day: the chapter whose number is the day
  of the month. A month with 31 days reads the whole book.
suits: Readers who want a short reading tied to the date, about one to
  three minutes, on its own or beside other reading.
schedule: day-of-month
behaviors: calendar
reading-days: 7
coverage: books
canon: protestant
books: PRO
limitations: It reads Proverbs only. A month with fewer than 31 days has no
  reading for the days it lacks, so chapter 31 is read in seven months of
  the year, and February has no reading for chapters 30 and 31, or for
  chapter 29 except in a leap year.
instructions: Read the chapter numbered for today's date, in any Bible. If
  you miss a day, read today's chapter; the one you missed stays in your
  history and comes round again next month.
source: An original schedule by Day by Word. Proverbs has 31 chapters, so
  each day of the month is given the chapter of the same number.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
